		"QG_TITLE": "How Tormenta Imperial works",
		"QG_OK": "Let's build!",
		"QG_RESOURCES_T": "Resources",
		"QG_RESOURCES_B": "Gold and wood from the start. Steel comes with your first Foundry (era 2) and oil with your first Refinery (era 3). Everything goes into one shared storehouse: what does not fit is lost, and each Warehouse adds 500. Your workers eat 1 gold and 1 wood per cycle.\n\nMaterials: planks, ingots, beams and fuel. Specialised buildings make them and advanced buildings need them. They are kept apart, in the workshop.",
		"QG_EXTRACT_T": "Extracting",
		"QG_EXTRACT_B": "Tap a forest, a vein or a well to work it by hand: resources right away, but it runs out.\n\nA specialised building next to it produces on its own without spending it, and makes its material: Sawmill by the forest, Gold Mine by the vein, Foundry by the iron, Refinery on the well. Use the vein up by hand and its building stops.",
		"QG_BUILDINGS_T": "Buildings and roads",
		"QG_BUILDINGS_B": "BUILD opens the list with each building's cost. Most need workers: each House brings 6.\n\nEvery building is joined to the Core by road. If none reaches it, one is laid when you place it (1 gold per tile, instantly). A building without a road does not work.",
		"QG_PROGRESS_T": "Progress",
		"QG_PROGRESS_B": "You move up an era by building: the Foundry opens era 2 (first: Sawmill, Gold Mine, House and Warehouse) and the Refinery era 3 (first: Foundry and Barracks).\n\nAt the Laboratory you research permanent advantages; at the Market you buy and sell. The Storm keeps coming back for the Tithe: the Barracks and the Towers defend it. WHAT NOW? always tells you the next step.",
