		# Tech Tree
		"BTN_TECH": "TECH",
		"LBL_TECH_TITLE": "Tech Tree",
		# Arbol explicado: que da cada tecnologia y que es en el mundo
		"LBL_TECH_INTRO": "Research PERMANENT advantages here. Each one costs resources and time, and only one is researched at a time. Three branches (Industrial, Military, Logistics) of five tiers, in order: tier 2 needs tier 1.\nIn the world: the Regency wrote us off and took the blueprints with it. This is what the Written-Off reinvent on their own.",
		"LBL_TECH_ADVANTAGE": "Advantage: %s",
		"TECH_ADV_PRODUCTION": "+%d%% production in every building",
		"TECH_ADV_STORAGE": "+%d shared storage",
		"TECH_ADV_SPREAD": "-%d points of Market spread",
		"TECH_ADV_MORALE": "+%d morale per fully paid cycle",
		"TECH_ADV_CONSUMPTION": "-%d%% of what each worker consumes",
		"TECH_ADV_BUILD": "-%d%% construction time",
		"TECH_BRANCH_INDUSTRIAL_DESC": "Production, storage and consumption. The factories the Empire dismantled when it left, rebuilt from memory.",
		"TECH_BRANCH_MILITARY_DESC": "Morale: people recover faster when everything is paid. A colony that knows it is defended takes the bill better.",
		"TECH_BRANCH_LOGISTICS_DESC": "Market, storage and build speed. Routes and depots that are not in the Ledger.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_1": "Imperial factory manuals, copied by hand from a volume the Ledger lists as destroyed.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_2": "Depots that appear on no plan. What is not in the Ledger is not assessed.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_3": "Double shifts and boilers at working pressure. The Regency would call it yield; here we call it eating.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_4": "Ration cards weighed to the gram. We learned their bookkeeping and now we keep it ourselves.",
		"TECH_LORE_ind_5": "Machines that neither tire nor depreciate. What the Empire denied us, rebuilt from scrap.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_1": "Falling in without uniform or flag. A people struck from the census can still take roll call.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_2": "Drill with salvaged rifles. The Assessors bring an escort; so do we.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_3": "Studying how the Assessors collect: where they come in, what they look at first, how long they stay.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_4": "Sandbags and riveted plate. A colony that defends itself stops being an entry in the Ledger.",
		"TECH_LORE_mil_5": "We no longer ask not to be collected. We decide who comes in.",
		"TECH_LORE_log_1": "Smugglers who know the gaps in the blockade. The Imperial Exchange charges less to those who know the way in.",
		"TECH_LORE_log_2": "Depots scattered across the island. One warehouse gets assessed whole; ten hidden ones do not.",
		"TECH_LORE_log_3": "Prefabricated parts and crews on a timetable. If they arrive on schedule, so do we.",
		"TECH_LORE_log_4": "Deciding who we sell to and at what price. \"Nothing is lost\", says the Regency. Nor here.",
		"TECH_LORE_log_5": "Our own routes, depots and works. For the first time, we are the ones keeping the ledger.",
