		"LBL_TUTORIAL_PAGE": "%d / %d",
		"LBL_TUTORIAL_SECTION_LORE": "THE WORLD",
		"LBL_TUTORIAL_SECTION_PLAY": "HOW TO PLAY",
		"TUT_INTRO_1_TITLE": "The Empire Without Sunset",
		"TUT_INTRO_1_BODY": "That is what it calls itself: the Empire Without Sunset, the one the sun never sets on.\n\nIt is true. Over them, it never does.\n\nOver us, it has not risen in three generations. We live under a roof of ash they manufacture and dispatch, in a permanent rust-coloured dusk. They divided up the light of the world and kept all of it.\n\nTheir motto: \"Wherever the light reaches\". What it really means: as far as they decide it should.",
		"TUT_INTRO_2_TITLE": "The Perpetual",
		"TUT_INTRO_2_BODY": "The Empire is ruled by the Perpetual, emperor by eternal right.\n\nNo one has seen him in a hundred and fourteen winters. No new portraits. No speeches. There are signatures: thousands upon thousands, all identical, on every tribute order, every sentence and every storm dispatch.\n\nThe Perpetual is dead, and has been for a century.\n\nThey do not hide it out of devotion. They hide it out of arithmetic: announcing a death opens a succession, a succession is a war, and a war interrupts collection. A dead emperor never changes his mind and never forgives a debt. He is the perfect ruler. That is why they keep him.",
		"TUT_INTRO_3_TITLE": "The Regency",
		"TUT_INTRO_3_BODY": "If the emperor does not rule, someone does.\n\nThe Regency was founded as a temporary measure to administer the Empire in the Perpetual's absence. That was a hundred and fourteen winters ago. It is still temporary.\n\nIt is not an army or a court: it is an accounting house. Lifelong clerks who do not conquer territories, they register them. Who do not declare wars, they suspend supplies. Who know exactly how much grain every province holds and how long every province lasts without it.\n\nTheir motto: \"Nothing is lost\". It sounds like comfort. It is an inventory.",
		"TUT_INTRO_4_TITLE": "The Storm is not weather",
		"TUT_INTRO_4_BODY": "People believe the Storm is weather. A punishment of the world, the bad luck of being born downwind. They pray to it. They endure it.\n\nThe Storm is not weather. It is mail.\n\nAcross the ocean stand the Chimneys: an artificial mountain range whose only purpose is to push the air. All the slag of the Empire is loaded onto the wind and dispatched. And it leaves on schedule.\n\nThey do not send it to dirty us. They send it to soften us. With the ash come the Assessors: armed appraisers who look at your stores, write it down and take their share. They call it the Tithe. First the ruin, then the bill. Always in that order.",
		"TUT_INTRO_5_TITLE": "Us: the Written-Off",
		"TUT_INTRO_5_BODY": "They did not defeat us. They wrote us off.\n\nThree generations ago, a clerk we never met made a calculation we never saw and decided this island had stopped being profitable. We appear in the Ledger as an accepted loss. They stopped counting us. And we survived.\n\nWhat is not in the Ledger is not collected. That invisibility was the only good thing that ever happened to us.\n\nBut we have grown. Chimneys can be seen from the sea. And the Regency, which never forgives a miscalculation, has opened the page again.\n\nGrowing is what makes you visible. Being visible is what brings the Storm.",
		"TUT_INTRO_6_TITLE": "On the mud of history",
		"TUT_INTRO_6_BODY": "\"On the mud of history, we shall build monuments of steel.\"\n\nThis is what you have: a Core, three hundred gold, two hundred wood and an island the Empire struck out.\n\nBuild. Grow. And when the air comes in dirty from the east, let it find you ready.\n\nNext: how to play.",
		"TUT_PLAY_1_TITLE": "The Core and the first works",
		"TUT_PLAY_1_BODY": "The Core is your centre. It cannot be demolished and it never falls.\n\nFirst, always: a sawmill. Without wood there is nothing, and everything that follows costs it. Place it right next to a forest: extractors go beside their deposit, just as the gold mine goes beside a vein.\n\nThen a house. Almost every building needs people to run it; without workers it stands idle.\n\nBUILD button at the bottom. WASD or drag to move the camera, wheel to zoom, R to rotate before placing.",
		"TUT_PLAY_2_TITLE": "One single bag",
		"TUT_PLAY_2_BODY": "Your four resources (gold, wood, steel and oil) share ONE single storage bag. When it is full, whatever you produce is lost. Spend, or build warehouses.\n\nYour people eat: each person consumes 1 wood and 1 gold per cycle. If you cannot pay, morale collapses.\n\nMorale multiplies your production: at 0 you produce half, at 100 twenty percent more. When you grow, grow wood first.",
		"TUT_PLAY_3_TITLE": "The Storm can be seen coming",
		"TUT_PLAY_3_BODY": "The Storm does not hit at once. It has phases, and the sky indicator tells you which:\n\nWARNING: ash on the horizon. Nothing falls yet.\nASH: production drops, and whatever is queued will be lost.\nSTORM: it breaks buildings.\nTITHE: the Assessors arrive to collect.\n\nSpend beforehand what you do not want taken. Repair afterwards what broke. And keep a garrison: if the Assessors meet resistance, it is fought on the board, and if you win they take nothing.",
		"TUT_PLAY_4_TITLE": "Towers and garrison",
		"TUT_PLAY_4_BODY": "Standing towers soften the Storm's damage, and their crews fight when the Assessors arrive.\n\nThe Barracks trains units: infantry, artillery and vehicles. Each barracks trains one at a time, and all of them draw wages in gold.\n\nOn the board: a unit moves and then attacks. Artillery cannot fire at an enemy adjacent to it. Defending doubles defence until your next turn.\n\nThe path: sawmill, houses, mine, foundry (era 2), barracks, refinery on an oil well (era 3), towers, Headquarters. At level 3 it summons the Regency's final audit. Survive it.",
		"TUT_TIP_INCOMING_TITLE": "Warning: ash on the horizon",
		"TUT_TIP_INCOMING_BODY": "The air is coming in dirty from the east. Nothing falls yet, but it will.\n\nNow: spend what you do not want taken, repair what is damaged and make sure you have a garrison. The Assessors collect on whatever they find in your stores.",
		"TUT_TIP_ASH_TITLE": "Ash is falling",
		"TUT_TIP_ASH_BODY": "Production drops while it lasts. And beware: running processes and units in training will be lost when the Storm hits. Finish what you can and start nothing new.",
		"TUT_TIP_STORM_TITLE": "Storm",
		"TUT_TIP_STORM_BODY": "Now it breaks buildings. Standing towers soften the damage. A building that reaches zero is left in ruins and stops producing until you repair it. Hold on: it passes.",
		"TUT_TIP_TITHE_TITLE": "The Assessors",
		"TUT_TIP_TITHE_BODY": "They have come to collect the Tithe. Your garrison fights on the board. If you win, they take nothing. If you lose, or have nothing to fight with, they take a percentage of your stores.",
		"TUT_TIP_RUINED_TITLE": "A building in ruins",
		"TUT_TIP_RUINED_BODY": "In ruins it produces nothing. It stays where it is: click the building and press REPAIR. It costs resources, but less than building it again.",
		"TUT_TIP_OVERFLOW_TITLE": "The bag is full",
		"TUT_TIP_OVERFLOW_BODY": "Your four resources share one single bag, and whatever does not fit is lost. Spend on buildings or build a warehouse: each one raises the cap by 500.",
		"TUT_TIP_BOARD_TITLE": "The board",
		"TUT_TIP_BOARD_BODY": "Turn-based, in initiative order. A unit may move and then attack; attacking ends its turn. Artillery cannot fire at an enemy adjacent to it. Defending doubles defence until your next turn.",
		# Helper callout: Skirmish button (appears with the first Barracks)
		"LBL_HELP_SKIRMISH": "SKIRMISH: from here you send expeditions with your army and, when ready, summon the Final Audit.",

