		"TECH_BLOCK_COST": "Missing: %s",
		"TUT_TIP_BARRACKS_TITLE": "The Barracks",
		"TUT_TIP_BARRACKS_BODY": "Trains infantry (era 1), artillery (era 2) and vehicles (era 3). Each barracks trains one unit at a time and you pay up front: open ARMY in ☰ MENU.\n\nTroops at home defend against the Tithe. From SKIRMISHES they march out on expeditions for loot.",
		"TUT_TIP_MARKET_TITLE": "The Imperial Exchange",
		"TUT_TIP_MARKET_BODY": "Buy and sell against gold. Buying pushes the price up and selling pushes it down; over time it drifts back. You always buy dearer than you sell: use it to plug a gap, not to live off it.",
		"TUT_TIP_TECH_TITLE": "The tech tree",
		"TUT_TIP_TECH_BODY": "It is researched at the Laboratory: tap it on the map. It grants permanent advantages: Industrial raises production (+10% already at tier 1) and storage, Military recovers morale faster and Logistics makes the Market cheaper and speeds up construction. Each tech states its advantage in numbers.\n\nIt costs resources and time, one at a time, and each branch goes in order: tier 2 needs tier 1. If one is greyed out, the reason is written under it.",
		"TUT_TIP_MAP_TITLE": "The expedition map",
		"TUT_TIP_MAP_BODY": "You advance left to right, one node per stage. Each node's risk is written under it: more risk, more enemies and more loot. Wounds do not heal between nodes. You can abandon and keep the loot; the boss waits at the end.",
		"TUT_TIP_UPKEEP_TITLE": "Paying the troops",
		"TUT_TIP_UPKEEP_BODY": "Every unit is paid in gold every 30 seconds. With no gold, the wages empty the till; if it keeps going unpaid, they desert, the most expensive first. Train what you can afford.",
		"TUT_TIP_CONSUMPTION_TITLE": "People eat",
		"TUT_TIP_CONSUMPTION_BODY": "Each worker consumes 1 wood and 1 gold per cycle. If it runs short, morale collapses and production with it; below 30 nobody is born. More sawmills and mines before more houses.",
		"TUT_TIP_AUDIT_TITLE": "The Regency is coming",
		"TUT_TIP_AUDIT_BODY": "The Headquarters at level 3 has called the Final Audit: 3 to 5 waves in a row against whoever is home, with no retraining in between. When you are ready, press LET THEM COME in SKIRMISHES.\n\nLosing does not end the game: it costs dearly, and you can try again.",
