		"PRO_1_TITLE": "The Emperor's signature",
		"PRO_1_BODY": "The Empire controls almost the whole world. Every order it gives carries the Emperor's signature.\n\nNo one has seen him in a hundred years. He has been dead for a century. The Regency rules in his name and signs for him. A dead emperor never changes his mind or forgives a debt.",
		"PRO_1_NOTE": "We have spent our whole lives obeying a dead man.",
		"PRO_1_STAMP": "SIGNED",
		"PRO_2_TITLE": "The Storm",
		"PRO_2_BODY": "Every so often, the sky fills with ash. That is the Storm. The Empire sends it to break what we build.\n\nBehind the ash come the Assessors. They count what is in the storehouses and take their share. They call it the Tithe. First comes the ruin, then the bill.",
		"PRO_2_NOTE": "The Storm is not weather: it is mail, and it always arrives on time.",
		"PRO_3_TITLE": "Who we are",
		"PRO_3_BODY": "We are the Written-Off. It is the Empire's name for what it gives up for lost. Three generations ago, it gave up this island. Those who could pay for a ship left. We stayed.\n\nNow smoke rises from our chimneys, and the Empire is looking again. We will build and survive every Storm. We will not pay the Tithe. And when they come down to collect, we will beat them.",
		"PRO_3_NOTE": "“On the mud of history, we shall build monuments of steel.”",
		"PRO_3_STAMP": "ALIVE",
		"PRO_B_TITLE": "Pending",
		"PRO_B_BODY": "Report from the coast watch: smoke where the ledger says no one lives.\n\nThe island is left off the dispatch route while the file is resolved. No ash and no Assessors will be sent.\n\nLet them build. There will be more to value later.",
		"PRO_B_NOTE": "The Storm does not reach us here. Build.",
		"PRO_B_STAMP": "PENDING",
