		"HELP_CAT_ARMY": "ARMY AND COMBAT",
		"HELP_T_BUILD": "Building",
		"HELP_B_BUILD": "BUILD (the big button at the bottom) opens the building list. Pick one and click on the map. Extractors go next to their deposit.",
		"HELP_B_BUILD_TOUCH": "BUILD (the big button at the bottom) opens the building list. Pick one, tap the map and confirm with ✓. Extractors go next to their deposit.",
		"HELP_T_OBJECTIVE": "Your objective",
		"HELP_B_OBJECTIVE": "Here is the next thing worth doing. Complete it and the next one appears.",
		"HELP_T_RESOURCES": "Resources and storage",
		"HELP_T_CAMERA": "Camera",
		"HELP_T_ZOOM": "Zoom and rotation",
		"HELP_T_MENUS": "☰ MENU",
		"HELP_B_MENUS": "☰ MENU pauses the game and has it all: What To Do, Progress, Market, Technology, Army, Save, Settings, HELP and Story.",
		"HELP_T_SKIRMISH": "Skirmishes",
		"HELP_B_FIRST_STEPS": "The Core is your centre: it cannot be demolished and it never falls.\n\nFirst, always, a sawmill right next to a forest. Extractors go beside their deposit, just as the gold mine goes beside a vein.\n\nThen a house. Almost every building needs people to run it: without workers it stands idle (Zzz).\n\nBUILD (bottom) opens the list. WASD or drag to move the camera, wheel to zoom, R to rotate before placing.",
		"HELP_B_FIRST_STEPS_TOUCH": "The Core is your centre: it cannot be demolished and it never falls.\n\nFirst, always, a sawmill right next to a forest. Extractors go beside their deposit, just as the gold mine goes beside a vein.\n\nThen a house. Almost every building needs people to run it: without workers it stands idle (Zzz).\n\nBUILD (bottom) opens the list. Drag a finger to move the camera, pinch to zoom and use ↻ to rotate before placing.",
		"HELP_B_STORM": "The Storm does not come in the first minute: it comes when your smoke can be seen from the sea, with industry. And it does not hit all at once: the sky indicator tells you the phase.\n\nWARNING: ash on the horizon, nothing falls yet.\nASH: production drops and anything queued will be lost.\nSTORM: it breaks buildings.\nTITHE: the Assessors come to collect.\n\nSpend beforehand what you do not want taken, repair afterwards what it breaks, and keep a garrison: win on the board and they take nothing.",
		"HELP_B_ARMY": "The path: sawmill, gold mine, house, another sawmill, warehouse, foundry (era 2), barracks, garrison, refinery on a well (era 3), two towers, Headquarters. The WHAT TO DO? panel always tells you the next step.\n\nGarrison: three infantry alone lose the Tithe. Five units, two of them artillery, win it. Standing towers soften the Storm and their crew fights.\n\nOn the board a unit moves, then attacks. Artillery cannot fire at an adjacent enemy. Defending doubles defence until your next turn.\n\nHeadquarters at level 3 summons the Final Audit. Six armoured vehicles at home win it almost every time.",
		"HELP_TIP_TITHE_BODY": "They have come to collect the Tithe. Your garrison fights on the board: win and they take nothing.\n\nLose, or have nothing to fight with, and they take a share of your storage; from the second visit on there is a Minimum Quota: if you cannot cover it, they seize buildings and workers.",
		"HELP_TIP_BARRACKS_BODY": "Trains infantry (era 1), artillery (era 2) and vehicles (era 3). Each barracks trains one unit at a time and you pay up front: open ARMY in the menu.\n\nFor the Tithe, three infantry alone always lose. Five units with two artillery win. From SKIRMISH they go on expeditions for loot.",
		"HELP_TIP_CONSUMPTION_BODY": "Every worker eats 1 wood and 1 gold per cycle. If it runs short, morale plunges and production with it; below 30 nobody is born.\n\nRight now: buy what is missing at the MARKET, or sell what is left over. Then more sawmills and mines before more houses.",
		"HELP_TIP_AUDIT_BODY": "Headquarters at level 3 has called the Final Audit: 3 to 5 waves in a row against whatever is at home, with no retraining in between. Six armoured vehicles win it almost every time; three units almost never.\n\nWhen you are ready, press LET THEM COME in SKIRMISH. Losing does not end the game: it costs dearly and you can try again.",
